WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.479 --> 00:00:01.312
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.312 --> 00:00:03.711
today's message is have goals.

00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:05.960
Over to you Eric Worre.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.736
(cockerel crows)

00:00:07.736 --> 00:00:10.276
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.946
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:16.446
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.454 --> 00:00:21.529
- My future plan is
about this thick, typed.

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:24.362
It's usually about 40 pages or so.

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:27.667
And it includes everything.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.844
And today, more than
ever, what you'll find

00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:34.190
with top leaders, what you'll
find with successful people,

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.773
is they're forward thinking,
they're future thinking

00:00:37.773 --> 00:00:41.441
and that future starts
to pull them towards

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.858
those objectives.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.130
So I set my goals pretty high

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.575
and I've set my calendar far in advance,

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:51.112
I'm planning, I still
have some spontaneity,

00:00:51.112 --> 00:00:54.445
room for spontaneity, but more and more,

00:00:57.647 --> 00:01:02.287
as the demands on my time
are growing exponentially,

00:01:02.287 --> 00:01:04.581
I have to plan and what I've,

00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:07.498
I've done this for, gosh, 25 years,

00:01:09.007 --> 00:01:11.280
so look back and look forward.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.021
Look back, take inventory, be honest,

00:01:14.021 --> 00:01:16.432
and look forward and map it out.

00:01:16.432 --> 00:01:19.356
So I want you to think about short-term,

00:01:19.356 --> 00:01:22.317
mid-term, long-term goals

00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:24.509
for you, personally and for your team.

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:26.446
- When you have specific goals,

00:01:26.446 --> 00:01:28.572
you're much more likely to follow through.

00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:30.435
When you know where you're going,

00:01:30.435 --> 00:01:32.684
and you've clearly defined it,

00:01:32.684 --> 00:01:36.257
you're much more likely to
achieve and hit that target.

00:01:36.257 --> 00:01:38.266
The challenge then becomes making sure

00:01:38.266 --> 00:01:41.198
you have meaningful
goals that support you.

00:01:41.198 --> 00:01:42.620
I look at my Mastermind Group,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.839
there's a collection of entrepreneurs,

00:01:43.839 --> 00:01:45.178
we get together once a month,

00:01:45.178 --> 00:01:47.786
and we have goals as a part of what we do.

00:01:47.786 --> 00:01:50.036
There's short-term goals, and
what you're going to get done

00:01:50.036 --> 00:01:53.106
before the end of next month,
so before you come and meet

00:01:53.106 --> 00:01:54.858
at the next meeting,
here are the three things

00:01:54.858 --> 00:01:56.704
that you need to do in your business

00:01:56.704 --> 00:01:59.627
and in your life to make
some forward progress.

00:01:59.627 --> 00:02:01.586
And it's self-defined, it's not
me saying here's your goals,

00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:03.017
you need to come with your goals

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.627
and say here's what I need to get done

00:02:04.627 --> 00:02:06.833
before the end of our next meeting

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.554
and then we have an annual goal.

00:02:08.554 --> 00:02:10.896
By December 31st of this year,

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.618
what does your business look like?

00:02:12.618 --> 00:02:15.346
And we force it to be a quantifiable goal,

00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:17.704
it has to be specific, we
have to be able to measure it,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.161
it's not just I want to
feel happy about my life,

00:02:20.161 --> 00:02:22.043
it's got to be something that's tangible.

00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:23.370
Most people pick a revenue goal

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.375
cos that's a significant,
meaningful goal in their business,

00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:27.717
it doesn't have to be revenue,

00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:29.457
but it has to be quantifiable.

00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:32.543
So I have goals, I have a goal

00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:34.814
to hit a million YouTube
subscribers on my channel,

00:02:34.814 --> 00:02:36.568
it's not just that that's
the goal that I want

00:02:36.568 --> 00:02:39.159
and when I accomplish
that, then it's game over,

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.830
then I've won, I still
respect and enjoy the process,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.893
I enjoy making the videos much more

00:02:44.893 --> 00:02:47.206
than just hitting that goal but that goal,

00:02:47.206 --> 00:02:49.539
allows me to align my plans.

00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:54.746
I have a goal to hit
gold in Living Legends

00:02:54.746 --> 00:02:57.951
and so I have a plan to
work on accomplishing that

00:02:57.951 --> 00:03:01.014
and not all of your goals
need to be growth-oriented,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.260
sometimes a goal is just
maintaining your habits.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.313
Now I have a goal to be a good husband.

00:03:06.313 --> 00:03:08.024
If that's your goal, just in itself,

00:03:08.024 --> 00:03:11.246
it's hard to live up to
because what does that mean?

00:03:11.246 --> 00:03:12.705
It's not specific enough.

00:03:12.705 --> 00:03:16.036
And so for me, there's three
things that I do everyday

00:03:16.036 --> 00:03:20.151
that's on my list, that
means being a good husband,

00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:21.572
things that are important to my wife

00:03:21.572 --> 00:03:24.831
and important for me and so I
try to do these three things

00:03:24.831 --> 00:03:26.955
every single day and when I do that,

00:03:26.955 --> 00:03:28.703
then I've kind of checked the boxes,

00:03:28.703 --> 00:03:31.151
like I'm doing the
things that I need to do

00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:32.538
to be a good husband.

00:03:32.538 --> 00:03:34.060
And so when you can quantify,

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.369
when you can get specific around the goal,

00:03:36.369 --> 00:03:39.162
you're much more likely
to accomplish that goal.

00:03:39.162 --> 00:03:41.381
The trick then becomes making sure

00:03:41.381 --> 00:03:43.354
that you have goals that support you

00:03:43.354 --> 00:03:45.475
in being that best version of yourself.

00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:48.740
Do you know what a good picture
looks like in the future?

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.714
Do you have a goal that is
motivating and meaningful to you?

00:03:51.714 --> 00:03:53.150
So as an example, I was listening

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:56.976
to a motivational DVD or CD, years ago

00:03:56.976 --> 00:03:59.187
and the guy's talking about goal setting

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:00.677
and he's talking about
write down your goals,

00:04:00.677 --> 00:04:02.861
and he's very energetic,
write down your goals,

00:04:02.861 --> 00:04:04.971
and, you know, if you
want to make a sculpture,

00:04:04.971 --> 00:04:06.901
write down make a sculpture,

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.957
if you want to make a painting,
write down make a painting

00:04:09.957 --> 00:04:14.124
and so, his energy influenced
me to want those things,

00:04:15.233 --> 00:04:17.192
yeah, yeah, I want to make a sculpture,

00:04:17.192 --> 00:04:19.812
write make a sculpture, I
want to make a painting too,

00:04:19.812 --> 00:04:21.023
look at how exciting that sounds,

00:04:21.023 --> 00:04:22.479
I want to make a painting

00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:24.780
and then when I came back to
it, at the end of the day,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.254
I don't really want to make a sculpture,

00:04:26.254 --> 00:04:27.583
I don't really want to make a painting

00:04:27.583 --> 00:04:31.167
and so having goals like that
didn't ultimately serve me

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.474
and so that's the trick, figuring out

00:04:33.474 --> 00:04:36.464
what are the goals that if
you accomplish these things,

00:04:36.464 --> 00:04:39.294
it's going to serve you
playing at the level

00:04:39.294 --> 00:04:40.803
that you want to play at,

00:04:40.803 --> 00:04:43.805
having the clarity to
understand where you want to go

00:04:43.805 --> 00:04:45.310
and writing those things down,

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.675
because if you can
accomplish those things,

00:04:47.675 --> 00:04:50.723
it means that you are living
the life that you want to live

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.430
and once you get really specific, again,

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.933
you're much more likely to follow through

00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:59.300
than if you have no
game plan and no goals.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.853
So the question of the day today is,

00:05:00.853 --> 00:05:04.394
I'm curious, what are three of your goals?

00:05:04.394 --> 00:05:06.229
In your life or in your business,

00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:07.957
what are three goals that if you hit,

00:05:07.957 --> 00:05:10.018
it's going to make you feel really good

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:11.323
and it's a sign that your life

00:05:11.323 --> 00:05:12.874
and your business are on track.

00:05:12.874 --> 00:05:14.484
Leave it in the comments below,

00:05:14.484 --> 00:05:15.734
super curious to find out,

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.303
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:05:17.303 --> 00:05:19.857
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Juha Sipinen,

00:05:19.857 --> 00:05:21.154
I hope I pronounced that okay,

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.475
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:23.475 --> 00:05:26.264
Your One Word, it really,
really, really means a lot to me

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:27.675
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:05:27.675 --> 00:05:30.301
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:05:30.301 --> 00:05:32.522
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:32.522 --> 00:05:33.978
and whatever your one word is,

00:05:33.978 --> 00:05:35.737
I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:35.737 --> 00:05:38.376
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:38.376 --> 00:05:40.429
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:40.429 --> 00:05:44.441
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:44.441 --> 00:05:45.676
- What's up Believe Nation,

00:05:45.676 --> 00:05:47.481
for those of you who
want a little more detail

00:05:47.481 --> 00:05:49.480
on creating goals and the importance

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.728
to your life and business,

00:05:50.728 --> 00:05:53.645
I think you're going to enjoy
these special bonus clips.

00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:54.586
- I want to talk a little bit about goals,

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:57.071
along the lines of how do you lose

00:05:57.071 --> 00:06:00.126
37 pounds and write a book?

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.477
I'm just going to kind of
give you that as an example.

00:06:02.477 --> 00:06:06.620
For 24 years of my adult life, by choice,

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.853
I weighed well over 200 pounds.

00:06:08.853 --> 00:06:11.088
I say by choice, because you see,

00:06:11.088 --> 00:06:14.529
I have never accidentally eaten anything.

00:06:14.529 --> 00:06:17.362
(audience laughs)

00:06:18.971 --> 00:06:21.564
I mean it's always been deliberate,

00:06:21.564 --> 00:06:24.739
and when I choose to eat too much today,

00:06:24.739 --> 00:06:28.156
I have chosen to weigh too much tomorrow.

00:06:30.079 --> 00:06:35.048
You can choose to set goals
and realize your potential

00:06:35.048 --> 00:06:37.372
or you can choose not to set them.

00:06:37.372 --> 00:06:38.987
Now, if you choose not to set them,

00:06:38.987 --> 00:06:41.522
you've got to understand
that the consequences

00:06:41.522 --> 00:06:44.872
are not going to be good down the road.

00:06:44.872 --> 00:06:48.624
For 24 years I was going
to lose that weight,

00:06:48.624 --> 00:06:50.156
as a matter of fact, in 24 years

00:06:50.156 --> 00:06:53.276
I lost several thousand pounds of weight.

00:06:53.276 --> 00:06:56.136
How many of you already know
exactly what I'm talking about?

00:06:56.136 --> 00:06:59.182
But it wasn't until I wrote it down,

00:06:59.182 --> 00:07:03.349
put a date on it, listed the
obstacles I had to overcome,

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:06.926
identified the people, the
groups, the organizations

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:11.736
I needed to work with,
spelled out a plan of action,

00:07:11.736 --> 00:07:14.553
set that time limit in there,

00:07:14.553 --> 00:07:17.394
and identified all of the benefits to me,

00:07:17.394 --> 00:07:19.252
it was only when I did that

00:07:19.252 --> 00:07:23.419
that the goal became a
reality and I lost the weight.

00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:27.403
For 10 or 15 years I was
going to write a book,

00:07:27.403 --> 00:07:28.492
you know anybody who's going to

00:07:28.492 --> 00:07:30.623
do just a whole lot of things, folks?

00:07:30.623 --> 00:07:31.742
I was going to write a book.

00:07:31.742 --> 00:07:35.536
But it wasn't until I
got busy writing the book

00:07:35.536 --> 00:07:37.232
and writing the plans first,

00:07:37.232 --> 00:07:40.943
before the book ever
materialized now if this sounds

00:07:40.943 --> 00:07:42.589
like I'm trying to sell
you on having goals,

00:07:42.589 --> 00:07:44.993
how many of you are getting close already?

00:07:44.993 --> 00:07:46.421
How many of you are becoming convinced

00:07:46.421 --> 00:07:49.383
quite quickly that you
need to have those goals?

00:07:49.383 --> 00:07:50.921
There's no question about it.

00:07:50.921 --> 00:07:53.461
The immortal J. C. Penney,
many, many years ago,

00:07:53.461 --> 00:07:57.031
said give me a stock clerk with a goal

00:07:57.031 --> 00:08:00.360
and I'll give you a
man who'll make history

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.027
but give me a man without a goal

00:08:04.164 --> 00:08:07.371
and I'll give you a stock clerk.

00:08:07.371 --> 00:08:11.381
Now the interesting thing is
goals do not care who has them

00:08:11.381 --> 00:08:14.134
and let me give you a classic
example of the way they work.

00:08:14.134 --> 00:08:17.301
In 1950, a war torn, devastated Japan,

00:08:18.952 --> 00:08:21.891
a nation that had lost an
incredibly high percentage

00:08:21.891 --> 00:08:25.301
of its young men, their
cities were in ruins,

00:08:25.301 --> 00:08:27.753
they'd been bombed out, but in 1950,

00:08:27.753 --> 00:08:31.104
they got together, they meaning
industry and government,

00:08:31.104 --> 00:08:32.825
got together and set a goal.

00:08:32.825 --> 00:08:34.494
The goal was, we're going
to be the number one

00:08:34.494 --> 00:08:36.865
nation in the world during the 1950s

00:08:36.865 --> 00:08:39.690
in the production of textiles.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.462
In 1959, ladies and gentlemen,

00:08:42.462 --> 00:08:44.623
they accomplished that objective.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:46.728
In 1960 they set another goal.

00:08:46.728 --> 00:08:48.985
We're going to be the number
one nation in the world

00:08:48.985 --> 00:08:50.611
in the production of steel.

00:08:50.611 --> 00:08:52.650
Now, when you understand
there's no iron ore

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.783
in Japan of any significance,

00:08:54.783 --> 00:08:57.279
there's no coal of any significance there,

00:08:57.279 --> 00:08:59.294
we're going to be the number
one nation in the world

00:08:59.294 --> 00:09:02.344
in the production of steel,
it seems like an absurd goal

00:09:02.344 --> 00:09:05.319
and yet they reached their objective,

00:09:05.319 --> 00:09:06.821
they'd taken all of the steps.

00:09:06.821 --> 00:09:09.024
In 1970, the Japanese set another goal,

00:09:09.024 --> 00:09:11.530
they said during the 70s,
we'll be the number one nation

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.440
in the world in the
production of automobiles.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.473
They missed it folks, one year.

00:09:17.473 --> 00:09:18.932
It took 'em until 1980.

00:09:18.932 --> 00:09:20.608
In 1980, they set another goal

00:09:20.608 --> 00:09:23.409
and this time their goal
was we're going to be

00:09:23.409 --> 00:09:24.705
the number one nation in the world

00:09:24.705 --> 00:09:27.827
in the production of
computers and electronics.

00:09:27.827 --> 00:09:29.771
Yes, indeed, ladies and gentlemen,

00:09:29.771 --> 00:09:33.648
you absolutely must have those goals.

00:09:33.648 --> 00:09:35.796
- The general principle
is I am pro goal, right?

00:09:35.796 --> 00:09:38.176
I am pro paramaters, you know?

00:09:38.176 --> 00:09:42.062
There is this good story in the book about

00:09:42.062 --> 00:09:43.872
a woman named Elise Blaha Cripe

00:09:43.872 --> 00:09:45.967
who is a serial crafter and
she makes all this stuff

00:09:45.967 --> 00:09:47.304
and she shares it with the world

00:09:47.304 --> 00:09:48.451
and she's incredibly prolific

00:09:48.451 --> 00:09:50.541
and her whole advice is,

00:09:50.541 --> 00:09:52.384
she says people are always telling you

00:09:52.384 --> 00:09:54.858
to think outside the
box, she says my advice,

00:09:54.858 --> 00:09:57.535
is to get in the box,
basically, make yourself a box,

00:09:57.535 --> 00:09:59.935
make yourself these parameters,
these goals, whatever,

00:09:59.935 --> 00:10:02.308
again, it's not something
that's being imposed on you,

00:10:02.308 --> 00:10:03.534
that's really the clear point,

00:10:03.534 --> 00:10:04.973
it's not like someone's
saying here's your goal,

00:10:04.973 --> 00:10:06.584
here's what you should do, no, it's you,

00:10:06.584 --> 00:10:08.533
things that you select for yourself

00:10:08.533 --> 00:10:11.684
but I believe there's so much possibility

00:10:11.684 --> 00:10:14.718
in those parameters, or
in those constraints,

00:10:14.718 --> 00:10:16.515
as we talked about, so whether it's

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:18.215
my goal is to climb Mount Everest

00:10:18.215 --> 00:10:19.834
or maybe it's the 10
mountains, or something,

00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:21.387
and stages are also good.

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:25.240
Set stages or milestones,
the levels in Mario Brothers,

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:28.362
for me, it was 50
countries, 100 countries,

00:10:28.362 --> 00:10:29.994
then it was every continent,

00:10:29.994 --> 00:10:32.967
once I'd finished all of
Africa, that was a big thing.

00:10:32.967 --> 00:10:34.265
So I do think it's important

00:10:34.265 --> 00:10:36.966
to celebrate small wins along the way.

